[0.000253,"o","\u001b[1;34m          Prerequisite: Remove the LVM Setup\u001b[0m                                                                            "]
[0.000057,"o","\u001b[1;34m          Pool two blank disks into one volume group that holds a file system and swap space\u001b[0m                            \u001b[1;34m        Steps\u001b[0m                                                                                                           \u001b[1;34m          1. Create an lvm partition using all of /dev/sdb, and another using all of /dev/sdc\u001b[0m"]
[0.000044,"o","                           "]
[0.000203,"o","\u001b[1;34m          2. Initialize both as physical volumes and create a volume group named vg_storage from them\u001b[0m"]
[0.000289,"o","                   \u001b[1;34m          3. Create a 1 GiB logical volume named lv_swap, and one named lv_records from the rest of the space\u001b[0m           \u001b[1;34m          4. Format lv_records with XFS and persistently mount it on /records\u001b[0m                                           "]
[0.000165,"o","\u001b[1;34m          5. Format lv_swap as swap space and persistently activate it\u001b[0m                                                  \u001b[1;34m          6. Verify with lsblk, df, and swapon --show\u001b[0m"]
